---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../components/Disclaimer.astro';
import AuthorByline from '../components/AuthorByline.astro';
import { BUSINESS, MEDICARE_2026, MEDICARE_2027 } from '../data/site';

const title = 'What Doesn’t Medicare Plan G Cover?';
const seoTitle = 'What Medigap Plan G Does Not Cover';
const description = 'Plan G pays most of what Original Medicare leaves behind, but not the Part B deductible, drug costs or routine dental, vision and hearing care.';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Does Plan G cover prescription drugs?', a: 'No. Medigap helps with Original Medicare’s costs. Drug coverage is separate: you can add a stand-alone Part D plan, or get drug coverage inside most Medicare Advantage plans.' },
  { q: 'Does Plan G pay the Part B deductible?', a: `No. You pay the yearly Part B deductible yourself: ${MEDICARE_2026.partBDeductible} in ${MEDICARE_2026.year} and ${MEDICARE_2027.partBDeductible} in ${MEDICARE_2027.year}. After that, Plan G pays the Part B coinsurance.` },
  { q: 'Does Plan G cover routine dental, vision or hearing aids?', a: 'No. Original Medicare does not cover them, and a Medigap plan does not add them. Stand-alone dental, vision and hearing plans, or some Medicare Advantage plans, are the usual ways to cover them.' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/what-medigap-plan-g-does-not-cover#webpage`,
      name: title,
      description,
      about: [{ '@type': 'Thing', name: 'Medigap', sameAs: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medigap' }],
      speakable: { '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification', cssSelector: ['.lead', 'h2'] },
    },
    { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} seoTitle={seoTitle} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <PageHero
    title={title}
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Medicare Plans', href: '/services' }, { label: 'Medicare Supplement Insurance (Medigap)', href: '/services/medicare-supplement' }, { label: 'What Plan G does not cover' }]}
  />

  <article class="py-14 lg:py-18">
    <div class="container-narrow prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-crst-primary prose-a:text-crst-accent">

      <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-crst-gold bg-navy-50 p-5">
        <p class="text-navy-800 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Medicare Supplement Insurance (Medigap) Plan G pays most of the costs Original Medicare leaves behind, but it does not pay the
          yearly Part B deductible, it does not cover prescription drugs, and it does not add routine dental, vision or hearing coverage.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="lead text-xl text-navy-700">
        Plan G is popular because it fills nearly every gap in Original Medicare’s cost-sharing. “Nearly” is the important word, so here
        is exactly where the line falls.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-500 -mt-2">
        Written by <a href="/about">Jim Farnham, MS, MBA</a> — Licensed Agent / Insurance Broker (NY license {BUSINESS.nyLicense}).
      </p>

      <h2>What Plan G does pay</h2>
      <p>
        Medigap is extra insurance from a private company that helps pay your share of out-of-pocket costs in Original Medicare. The
        <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap/basics/compare-plan-benefits" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Medicare.gov benefits chart</a>
        shows a standard Plan G paying:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Part A coinsurance and hospital costs, up to an additional 365 days after Medicare benefits are used</li>
        <li>Part B coinsurance or copayment</li>
        <li>Blood (the first 3 pints)</li>
        <li>Part A hospice care coinsurance or copayment</li>
        <li>Skilled nursing facility care coinsurance</li>
        <li>The Part A deductible</li>
        <li>Part B excess charges</li>
        <li>Foreign travel emergency care (80%, up to plan limits)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What Plan G does not pay</h2>
      <h3>The yearly Part B deductible</h3>
      <p>
        This is the one cost-sharing item Plan G leaves to you. It is {MEDICARE_2026.partBDeductible} in {MEDICARE_2026.year} and
        {MEDICARE_2027.partBDeductible} in {MEDICARE_2027.year}. Once you have paid it, Plan G pays the Part B coinsurance for the rest
        of the year. With High-Deductible Plan G, your Part B deductible payment counts toward the plan’s own deductible
        ({MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} in {MEDICARE_2026.year}).
      </p>

      <h3>Prescription drugs</h3>
      <p>
        Drug coverage is separate from Medigap. You can add a stand-alone
        <a href="/services/prescription-drug-plans">Part D prescription drug plan</a> to Original Medicare, or get drug coverage inside
        most Medicare Advantage plans. Even if you don’t take prescription drugs now,
        <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/part-d/what-drug-plans-cover" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Medicare suggests considering drug coverage</a>,
        and enrolling late can add a
        <a href="/medicare-part-d-late-enrollment-penalty">permanent penalty</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Routine dental, vision and hearing care</h3>
      <p>
        The benefits in the chart above are the standardized Medigap benefits, and routine dental, vision and hearing care are not among
        them. Original Medicare itself does not cover routine eye exams for glasses, hearing aids, or most dental care, and Medigap helps
        with Original Medicare’s costs rather than adding those benefits. Read
        <a href="/does-medicare-plan-g-cover-eye-exams-hearing-aids-dental">does Plan G pay for eye exams, hearing aids or dental care</a>
        for what Original Medicare does cover, and
        <a href="/services/dental-vision-hearing">how stand-alone dental, vision and hearing plans fit in</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Anything that Original Medicare doesn’t cover</h3>
      <p>
        You can only buy Medigap if you have Original Medicare, and a Medigap plan is built around that coverage. If a service falls
        outside both Original Medicare and the Medigap benefits list, Plan G does not pay for it. Ask before you rely on a service being
        covered.
      </p>

      <h2>Filling the gaps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Drugs:</strong> a stand-alone <a href="/services/prescription-drug-plans">Part D plan</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Dental, vision and hearing:</strong> a <a href="/services/dental-vision-hearing">stand-alone plan</a>, or some Medicare Advantage plans include these as extra benefits.</li>
        <li><strong>Hospital stays:</strong> some people look at <a href="/services/dental-vision-hearing">hospital indemnity coverage</a> as a cash benefit on top of their other coverage.</li>
        <li><strong>A lower premium:</strong> the <a href="/services/high-deductible-medicare-supplement">high-deductible version of Plan G</a> trades a higher deductible for a lower premium. See <a href="/medigap-plan-g-cost-new-york">what Plan G costs in New York</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((f) => (<div class="mb-5"><h3 class="text-xl">{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></div>))}

      <div class="not-prose my-10 rounded-xl bg-crst-primary p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-white font-heading text-lg mb-2 m-0">Not sure what your plan covers?</p>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mb-4 m-0">A no-cost, no-pressure review, by phone or Zoom screen-share.</p>
        <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneClean}`} class="btn-accent text-base px-7 py-3">Call {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
      </div>

      <AuthorByline />

      <div class="not-prose mt-8">
        <Disclaimer variant="tpmo" />
        <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Plan availability, benefits and costs vary and are not guaranteed. Figures shown are {MEDICARE_2026.year} and
          {MEDICARE_2027.year} amounts set by Medicare and change annually. This page is educational and not individualized advice.
          NY producer license #: {BUSINESS.nyLicense}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTASection headline="Let’s find the coverage that fits you" />
</BaseLayout>
